          "OBJ-6136-1.2.01-00"
        ],
        "text": "The United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) organise international development ambitions for 2030. The saved 2022 examination figure shows examples including No Poverty, Zero Hunger, Good Health and Well-being, Clean Water and Sanitation, Decent Work and Economic Growth, and Responsible Consumption and Production. The syllabus specifically names SDG 12. Sustainable development can be considered through linked economic, social and environmental pillars; a goal may contribute to more than one, so do not force every goal into only one pillar. Progress in one area can help another, but trade-offs still need a judgement about present and future needs.",
